Mechanisms, at source 4777a36b:
- crates/bbt-supervisor/src/protocol.rs:233,288,296,387 — ReadRingBatch / RingRead / RingReadResult / RingHistoryBatch; at most 8 members and 768 KiB encoded aggregate.
- supervisor.rs:941 — byte budget includes frame metadata; one oversized member becomes Limit without erasing fitting siblings.
- supervisor.rs:1283,1292 — all leaves are admitted/refused before waiting; remaining existing 128 IO credits are assigned in order; overflow returns member Busy without writer admission; admitted ready data stays charged until aggregate completion. One reply reserve, no new queue or pool.
- crates/bbt-mux/src/logic.rs:1643 — per-host lane indices forecast the existing global 3:1 parse order, including parked/no-gap rows, without scanning every seat for each read.
- logic.rs:5255,5410 — one bounded cached group per host; validate member identity and contiguous seat/generation/range before use; preserve unapplied boundary rows; Busy retains the original target; definitive refusal keeps its cursor and does not prevent healthy members from advancing. Parsing still consumes one page per turn. Singleton reads remain in explicit history and bootstrap/recovery.
- provider/shared.rs:87 — every member is checked before forwarding; a mixed/wrong-host group gets the named host-boundary refusal before any valid prefix is sent.
- seat_socket.rs:331 and logic.rs:4101 — live/unresponsive recovery is typed SeatListenerPending. A recovered seat remains available; one pending endpoint bind rotates per ordinary turn. No attachment/effect replay, global seat scan or sleep in production.
- tests/capture_busy.rs, capture_fairness.rs, common/capture_priority.rs, provider.rs, recovery.rs and socket_backlog.rs observe successful member pages and preserve existing Busy/outage/crash boundaries, page budgets, exactness/order assertions and deadlines.

Functional proof:
- Actual hot-ingest fixture, 967 synthetic views: one host = 121 requests (bound 121); two hosts = 122 (sum-of-host bounds 122); zero singleton hot calls; exact final sequence, byte-end and Screen against serial Playback for every seat. No 967-PTY fixture or time-based pass criterion.
- Five logic batch tests pass: those two sweeps; Busy/Gone/Stale/Limit isolation and unchanged refused cursors; boundary/generation/writer cache checks; exhaustive watched masks/streaks/parked hosts/no-gap rows against the actual scheduler.
- Four supervisor tests pass: aggregate/independent results, retained credit lifetime, exact encoded-byte bound, malformed structure, and partial/full 128-credit capacity. A full queue returns per-member Busy, not a parent refusal.
- Real capture/provider subset 13/0; watched-priority regression 1/0 with original sliding-window and page-budget assertions.
- Listener regression holds a duplicate fd across Logic recovery, observes typed pending plus a working snapshot, closes it, then observes the same endpoint/capability/generation rebound. Original dead-owned-socket test waits at most 5 s for observed ConnectionRefused before reclaiming; all inode/file/symlink checks remain.
- Socket flood now counts batch leaf pages. Final scoped run kept the 64 MiB digest, sequence/order, exit and tail checks: PASS in 72.94 s, unchanged 90 s no-progress watchdog.

